# Pinned rest-server release, by architecture.
#
# Ubuntu packages no distribution build under any name (checked 2026-08-18),
# so the module downloads a release tarball. An unverified binary serving your
# offsite backups is not a trade worth making, so every download is checked
# against a checksum recorded here.
#
# These checksums were taken from the project's SHA256SUMS, whose detached
# signature verified as a GOOD signature from:
#
#   CF8F 18F2 8445 7597 3F79  D4E1 91A6 868B D3F7 A907
#   Alexander Neumann <alexander@bumpern.de>   (restic maintainer)
#
# The signing key was fetched from https://restic.net/gpg-key-alex.asc - an
# independent channel from GitHub, which is what makes the check mean anything.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UPDATING THIS FILE  (do not shortcut the signature step)
#
#   V=0.15.0
#   B=https://github.com/restic/rest-server/releases/download/v$V
#   curl -fsSLO $B/SHA256SUMS -O $B/SHA256SUMS.asc
#   curl -fsSL https://restic.net/gpg-key-alex.asc | gpg --import
#   gpg --verify SHA256SUMS.asc SHA256SUMS      # must say "Good signature"
#   grep linux_ SHA256SUMS
#
# Copying a checksum from the release page without verifying the signature
# gives you no more assurance than downloading the binary unchecked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

RSRV_VERSION=0.14.0
RSRV_BASE=https://github.com/restic/rest-server/releases/download

# dpkg architecture | sha256 of rest-server_<version>_linux_<arch>.tar.gz
amd64|4c9c95bc079a0334e81fad379b19dc5c3353c71c2c88d652cafce2081c2b1c66
arm64|cef139cbe8b27b16bda731d17f093b0aa466b8c60b136c12d78b6f2bff3daf22
386|de12ba817a8153be2ba4cbe6ae51ad2ca4c26d8210084659c1f421839bdb49c7
